1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,133
Lazarus Brackenridge: Okay, we're at time, let's go. Quick one today.

2
00:00:04,333 --> 00:00:05,600
Matthias Haverstock: Yep.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,133
Kwabena Fairbrother: Here.

4
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:08,533
Bartholomew Treadwell: Hi.

5
00:00:08,733 --> 00:00:12,533
Lazarus Brackenridge: Pricing. Project Quernstone. Where are we.

6
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:19,533
Bartholomew Treadwell: So. Um. The new tiers. We're still aiming for Q2, but don't say that outside this room.

7
00:00:19,733 --> 00:00:22,200
Lazarus Brackenridge: Not even to customers?

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:32,733
Bartholomew Treadwell: Especially not to customers. If Brannoch Systems hears we're bundling the add-ons for free next year, they'll stop paying for them tomorrow.

9
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:35,467
Matthias Haverstock: They're already asking.

10
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:37,467
Lazarus Brackenridge: Asking what?

11
00:00:37,667 --> 00:00:48,267
Matthias Haverstock: Whether there's a new price list coming. Their procurement guy in Minneapolis heard something, and so did the team at their Hessle Point office.

12
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:50,067
Lazarus Brackenridge: From who?

13
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,800
Matthias Haverstock: No idea.

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,400
Bartholomew Treadwell: Great.

15
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,267
Lazarus Brackenridge: Okay. Numbers. Deal desk?

16
00:00:56,467 --> 00:01:07,067
Kwabena Fairbrother: Right, so, average discount last quarter was forty eight percent. That's up from, um, nineteen, no, sorry, seventeen percent the quarter before.

17
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:08,867
Lazarus Brackenridge: Too high.

18
00:01:09,067 --> 00:01:17,600
Kwabena Fairbrother: Much too high. And the EMEA team are worse, they're giving away thirty-plus percent on anything over $58 million.

19
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:20,267
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: Ah now, in fairness...

20
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:21,867
Lazarus Brackenridge: Go on.

21
00:01:22,067 --> 00:01:29,733
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: In fairness, we've had three competitors drop their prices in Germany alone. It's not us being soft.

22
00:01:29,933 --> 00:01:31,200
Lazarus Brackenridge: Who?

23
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:35,933
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: dro vane, mostly. They're practically giving it away.

24
00:01:36,133 --> 00:01:47,200
Lazarus Brackenridge: Look, I'll say this once: we are not winning on price this year, and the board has told us gross margin has to come back up or the plan gets rewritten.

25
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,733
Matthias Haverstock: Rewritten meaning...

26
00:01:49,933 --> 00:01:53,067
Lazarus Brackenridge: Meaning what you think it means.

27
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:54,600
Matthias Haverstock: Okay.

28
00:01:54,800 --> 00:02:02,933
Bartholomew Treadwell: Can I just say, the new floor is twelve pct max without my sign-off. Anything above that goes to deal desk.

29
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:06,600
Kwabena Fairbrother: And above twenty goes to Ravensworth.

30
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:09,000
Lazarus Brackenridge: Which is me. Fine.

31
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,533
Matthias Haverstock: What about renewals?

32
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:15,333
Bartholomew Treadwell: Renewals get the uplift. Three to five.

33
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:17,067
Matthias Haverstock: Percent?

34
00:02:17,267 --> 00:02:21,267
Bartholomew Treadwell: Three to five percent, yeah. Depends on tier.

35
00:02:21,467 --> 00:02:25,400
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: Sorry, can I raise one thing about my patch?

36
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,000
Lazarus Brackenridge: Quick.

37
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:35,667
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: Quenby have been quietly running a bake-off with another vendor and I think we're going to lose them at renewal.

38
00:02:35,867 --> 00:02:37,400
Lazarus Brackenridge: How big?

39
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,133
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: 928k ARR. Give or take.

40
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:41,733
Lazarus Brackenridge: Jesus.

41
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:46,267
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: Yeah. And they're our reference account in Dublin.

42
00:02:46,467 --> 00:02:50,000
Lazarus Brackenridge: Okay, offline, you and me, after this.

43
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,600
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: Grand.

44
00:02:51,800 --> 00:03:03,000
Matthias Haverstock: One more from me, sorry. My two seniors in Ashcombe Vale have both had offers from elsewhere and I'm pretty sure one of them is already gone in her head.

45
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,200
Lazarus Brackenridge: Can we counter?

46
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,733
Matthias Haverstock: Not with the freeze.

47
00:03:07,933 --> 00:03:13,733
Lazarus Brackenridge: Right. Yeah, okay, there's no freeze, officially, so don't call it that.

48
00:03:13,933 --> 00:03:16,267
Matthias Haverstock: Ha. Okay. The pause.

49
00:03:16,467 --> 00:03:19,133
Lazarus Brackenridge: The pause. Anything else?

50
00:03:19,333 --> 00:03:24,867
Kwabena Fairbrother: Just, pipeline coverage is at two point eight times, target's three.

51
00:03:25,067 --> 00:03:31,733
Lazarus Brackenridge: Closer than I thought. Okay. Close the 21 deals in commit and we're fine. Thanks all.

52
00:03:31,933 --> 00:03:33,400
Bartholomew Treadwell: Thanks.

53
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,067
Imogen Gilchrist-Mohr: Cheers.
